<title>DENMARK: Clinton leaves Denmark after 20-hour visit.</title>
<headline>Clinton leaves Denmark after 20-hour visit.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1997-07-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. President Bill Clinton left Denmark on Saturday after a 20-hour visit, the first ever to a Scandinavian country by a serving U.S. president.</p>
<p>Clinton left aboard Air Force One at 5.15 pm (1515 GMT) from Copenhagen international airport bound for Washington after delivering a public speech to an enthusiastic crowd in a central Copenhagen square.</p>
